This product is a System One (Jev-like) decision engine. Its design and
implementation build on techniques validated by the following open-source
projects (each remains under its own license):

- jev-on-a-laptop (MIT)
  Parallel constrained decoding of typed decisions on stock LLMs.
  https://github.com/rorshopping/jev-on-a-laptop

- vllm-jev-decison (MIT)
  Classification-only typed decisions over raw model logprobs.
  https://github.com/siliconkernel/vllm-jev-decison

- openJev-verdict-2.0 (Apache-2.0)
  Non-autoregressive decision engine (ModernBERT + RLCD-style calibration).
  https://github.com/Heman10x-NGU/openJev-verdict-2.0

- LLaDA: Large Language Diffusion Models (Apache-2.0)
  Background on diffusion / masked parallel decoding.
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.09992

